{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"/*\\n    This program solves Laplace's equation on a regular 2D grid using simple Jacobi iteration.\\n\\n    The stencil calculation stops when  ( err >= CONV_THRESHOLD OR  iter > ITER_MAX )\\n*/\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <time.h>\\n#include <sys/time.h>\\n\\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f // threshold of convergence\\n\\n// matrix to be solved\\ndouble **grid;\\n\\n// auxiliary matrix\\ndouble **new_grid;\\n\\n// size of each side of the grid\\nint size;\\nint iter_max_num;\\n\\n// return the absolute value of a number\\ndouble absolute(double num){\\n    if(num < 0)\\n        return -1.0 * num;\\n    return num;\\n}\\n\\n\\n// allocate memory for the grid\\nvoid allocate_memory(){\\n    grid = (double **) malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\\n    new_grid = (double **) malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\\n\\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\\n        grid[i] = (double *) malloc(size * sizeof(double));\\n        new_grid[i] = (double *) malloc(size * sizeof(double));\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// initialize both buffers identically so untouched boundaries remain valid after swaps\\nvoid initialize_grid(){\\n    int center = size / 2;\\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++){\\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++){\\n            // inicializa região de calor no centro do grid\\n            double value;\\n            if ( i >= linf && i <= lsup && j >= linf && j <= lsup)\\n                value = 100;\\n            else\\n                value = 0;\\n            grid[i][j] = value;\\n            new_grid[i][j] = value;\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// save the grid in a file\\nvoid save_grid(){\\n\\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\\n        for(int j = 0; j < size; j++){\\n            fprintf(stdout, \\\"%lf \\\", grid[i][j]);\\n        }\\n        fprintf(stdout, \\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]){\\n\\n    fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &size);\\n    fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &iter_max_num);\\n    \\n    int hasError = 1;\\n    int iter = 0;\\n\\n    struct timeval time_start;\\n    struct timeval time_end;\\n\\n    // allocate memory to the grid (matrix)\\n    allocate_memory();\\n\\n    // set grid initial conditions\\n    initialize_grid();\\n\\n    //printf(\\\"Jacobi relaxation calculation: %d x %d grid\\\\n\\\", size, size);\\n\\n    // get the start time\\n    //gettimeofday(&time_start, NULL);\\n\\n    // Jacobi iteration\\n    // This loop will end if either the maximum change reaches below a set threshold (convergence)\\n    // or a fixed number of maximum iterations have completed\\n    while ( hasError && iter < iter_max_num ) {\\n\\n        hasError = 0;\\n        // Share stencil rows statically; the reduction combines convergence flags across threads.\\n        #pragma omp parallel if(size >= 64) reduction(|:hasError)\\n        {\\n            // calculates the Laplace equation to determine each cell's next value\\n            #pragma omp for schedule(static)\\n            for( int i = 1; i < size-1; i++) {\\n                for(int j = 1; j < size-1; j++) {\\n\\n                    new_grid[i][j] = 0.25 * (grid[i][j+1] + grid[i][j-1] +\\n                                             grid[i-1][j] + grid[i+1][j]);\\n\\n                    double errorCurrent = absolute(new_grid[i][j] - grid[i][j]);\\n                    if(errorCurrent > CONV_THRESHOLD ){\\n                        hasError = 1;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        // Both buffers have identical boundaries; swapping replaces the interior copy pass.\\n        double **tmp = grid;\\n        grid = new_grid;\\n        new_grid = tmp;\\n        iter++;\\n    }\\n\\n    // get the end time\\n    //gettimeofday(&time_end, NULL);\\n\\n    //double exec_time = (double) (time_end.tv_sec - time_start.tv_sec) +\\n    //                   (double) (time_end.tv_usec - time_start.tv_usec) / 1000000.0;\\n\\n    //save the final grid in file\\n    save_grid();\\n\\n    //printf(\\\"\\\\nKernel executed in %lf seconds with %d iterations.\\\\n\\\", exec_time, iter);\\n\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/laplace_seq.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"Combining static OpenMP row worksharing and convergence reduction with buffer swapping should retain parallel stencil updates while eliminating the interior copy pass. Identical initialization keeps untouched boundaries correct after every swap; the size threshold avoids team overhead on small grids.\",\"notes\":\"One integrated candidate for controller evaluation; no commands or measurements were run.\",\"sources_kept\":[\"11ce495741b04b02\",\"686876c0b37b4477\"],\"transformations\":[\"Use static OpenMP worksharing for the stencil rows, reduce hasError with bitwise OR, and serialize parallel execution below 64 rows.\",\"Initialize both buffers identically, including boundaries, and swap their pointers after every completed sweep instead of copying interior values.\"]}"}}
